Bootstrap: docker
From: python:3.11-slim-bookworm

%labels
    Maintainer sdweave2@ncsu.edu
    Source https://github.com/AnantharamanLab/CheckAMG
    Version 1.1.2

%help
    CheckAMG — automated discovery and curation of Auxiliary Metabolic Genes
    (AMGs), Auxiliary Regulatory Genes (AReGs), and Auxiliary Physiology
    Genes (APGs) encoded by viral genomes.

    CheckAMG supports both CPU-only and GPU-accelerated execution. The
    `de-novo` module (protein genome language model embedding + nearest-
    neighbor search) benefits from GPU acceleration; the `annotate` module
    (HMM-based) is CPU-bound.

    GPU usage: this container must be run on a GPU-attached node with
    --nv so the host NVIDIA driver is bound in:
        apptainer run --nv CheckAMG-1.1.2.sif <args>
    CPU-only usage works with a plain `apptainer run` (no --nv needed).

    Before first use, download the reference databases (~116 GB, or
    ~21 GB with --rm-hmm and excluding the de-novo module's database):
        apptainer run CheckAMG-1.1.2.sif download -d /path/to/db/destination --rm-hmm

    Modules:
        annotate   Predict and curate AVGs from functional annotations
                   (HMM searches) and viral genome context.
        de-novo    Embed query proteins with the PST genome language model
                   and predict AVGs via nearest-neighbor search; more
                   sensitive but does not assign specific functions.

    Example:
        apptainer run --nv CheckAMG-1.1.2.sif --help

%post -c /bin/bash
    set -e
    export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive

    # Hazel bind-mount points
    mkdir -p /rs1 /share /home /usr/local/usrapps

    apt-get update -qq && \
        apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
            build-essential \
            git \
            ca-certificates && \
        apt-get clean && \
        rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

    python3 -m pip install --no-cache-dir --upgrade pip setuptools wheel packaging uv

    # torch must be installed before torch_geometric/torch_scatter/CheckAMG
    # so the correct build is selected (per upstream README). Plain pip
    # resolution (no --index-url override) pulls PyPI's default Linux
    # wheel, which bundles CUDA runtime libs, so apptainer run --nv works
    # at run time without needing an nvidia/cuda base image.
    uv pip install --system --no-cache-dir torch==2.8.0
    uv pip install --system --no-cache-dir torch_geometric
    uv cache clean torch_scatter 2>/dev/null || true
    uv pip install --system --no-cache-dir torch_scatter --no-build-isolation --no-binary torch_scatter --refresh
    uv pip install --system --no-cache-dir faiss-cpu

    uv pip install --system --no-cache-dir checkamg==1.1.2

%environment
    export LC_ALL=C.UTF-8
    export LANG=C.UTF-8

%runscript
    exec checkamg "$@"

%test
    checkamg --help
